WEBVTT

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.420
Vice-principal, there's
an incoming message from a patrol ship.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.920
April 14th 10:30

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.510
From: Fifth Squad, Ship Two.
To: The Flagship Aotsuki.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.090
Musashi discovered.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.470
Higashi-Maizuru (Toumai)
Boys Marine High School Instructor Ship

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.810
Cruising at northern latitude of 19.41 degrees,
eastern longitude of 145.0 degrees.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.270
Attempts to contact them
on the radio, but no response.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.270
The beacon response is also off,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.150
so it's likely they're suffering
from electrical failure, including the radio.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.400
Contact the Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School
and let's give them the Musashi's position.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.530
Well, good thing they've been found.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.910
I'm sure they must've been really worried.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.000
We say maintaining students' safety
is what's most important,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.870
but to see multiple training vessels
go missing simultaneously.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:51.760
Fortunately, all of our students aboard
the I-201 were safely rescued, but...

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.760
And supposedly the Harekaze
engaged in battle with an instructor ship.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.800
What is going on?

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:06.060
Well, whatever is happening, let's go
and secure the Musashi immediately.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.150
Call the patrol ship back.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.040
Macchi!

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.670
Cool!

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.210
Awesome!

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.670
So amazing.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:02:59.880
Dolphins!

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.340
Dolphins in the flesh!

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.680
Break Until 12:00!

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.940
Hey, you didn't do your warm up exercises.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.320
Don't just jump in like that!

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.440
But dolphins!

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.700
Distance to the subject, 5.0.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.780
Two meters, 30 centimeters long?

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.200
- Boom.
- It's gonna go bang?

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.580
Rotate 120 degrees!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.120
Amazing! The open sea is amazing!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.630
Should we really be relaxing like this?

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.960
Ever since the entrance ceremony, it's been
one nerve-racking moment after another.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.720
So I thought it'd be okay
if we enjoyed ourselves a little.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.220
A little too much, probably.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.260
They're all relieved.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.850
We didn't mutiny at all,

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.890
and they seem to understand that now.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.520
Nonetheless, shouldn't we be
returning to school?

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.030
Ms. Hiraga and the others
are still interviewing Tama,

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.990
and the boiler's temperature
isn't finished rising.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.120
Damn you! Rise!

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.250
We can't leave right away.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.290
Okay, cheese!

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.510
Still, we should get back as soon as possible.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.680
I wonder if the Akashi
and the Mamiya arrived yet.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:28.560
What?

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.850
At the Musashi...

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.820
This month's fortune...

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.610
Scorpio is ninth place.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.820
Taurus is 11th.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.490
At least it's not last place, right?

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.490
By the way, what place is Gemini?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:48.620
12th place.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.450
It says you'll especially be unlucky near water.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.120
Sorry, sorry.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.630
I'm so unlucky.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.630
The fortune is right on!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.970
There's a psychology test, too.
Want to try it, Ms. Munetani?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:05.970
No!

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.680
Do you want to try it, Ms. Shiretoko?

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.560
M-Me?

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.770
Organization and Orderliness.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:23.780
Lucky ducks are so lucky.
I want to run around and have fun too.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.360
We're almost done here,
so hang in there a little more.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.330
Ms. Tateishi, I'm going to ask you once more.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:34.660
You can't remember why
you suddenly attacked the ships?

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.040
Aye.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.500
Don't blame yourself
if you can't remember, Tama.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:43.800
I would've fired too
if I had the chance in that situation.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.090
Shall we wrap it up?

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.020
I'll summarize our interview and report it
to the Maritime Safety Support Department.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.820
The Sarushima was the first one
to report the Harekaze's mutiny, right?

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.610
How did you conclude it was mutiny?

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.120
The Harekaze was late
to the training's rendezvous point,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:17.170
so when they arrived in the area,
we began the attack.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.380
The Harekaze retaliated
with a torpedo that struck our ship.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:24.170
I considered that to be mutiny
and reported it as such.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:27.630
Why did you attack them
for the minor offense of being tardy?

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.260
That is...

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:33.560
All the crew members have testified
that the captain ordered it.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:38.900
I remember giving the order.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:46.740
But I don't even know myself
how I came to that decision.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.610
This is Inspector Munetani.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:54.160
Good work.
I brought a treat.

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.000
Thank you.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:00.710
I would also like to speak
with Instructor Furushou.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.250
- May I have a few minutes?
- Of course.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.220
Are you okay, Furushou-senpai?

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:14.430
I heard you were adrift until being rescued.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.270
It's pathetic when you
have your junior worry about you.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.100
Thank you. I'm all right.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:26.440
Sorry. You'll have to stay here
until the investigation is completed.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.360
Please, have some.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:30.660
Thank you.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:40.460
I fired upon students
and can't remember why I did it.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.750
I'm furious with myself.

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:47.630
The other crew members also testified
that they remember clearly

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:52.430
of what had happened,
but can't recall why they did it.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.800
It's not just you, senpai.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:00.940
We salvaged the Sarushima's tactical data
processing system's log, but it was deleted.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:00.270
Nishinoshima Destroyer Harekaze
Torpedo Incident - Preliminary Research Report

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.770
The log's... gone.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:10.990
Looks like loss of function from 13:20.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.790
Is the Harekaze really okay?

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.170
Everyone is unharmed
from the captain on down.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.670
Excuse me.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.800
<i>From: Mayuki Munetani
Contact from Toumai. Informing you as well.</i>

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:35.220
<i>From: Toumai Boys' High
To: Yokosuka Girls' High
Musashi discovered. On the way to secure it.</i>

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:40.430
Sorry, senpai. Something has come up.

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:43.270
I hope you enjoy what I brought.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.780
It's kind of small.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:59.040
Hi. Don't the Budgeting people
get to have fun?

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.410
Y-Yeah. We will later.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.840
Am I being avoided?

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.340
The interview is over,
so we'll be taking our leave.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:16.640
When you return to port, the school will pass
the official punishment for firing the weapon,

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.060
but since there was no damage,
you might be let off with a stern warning.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.520
Thank you!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:23.770
Well then.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.770
Tama! You must be exhausted.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.070
Aye.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.570
It's all right, Tama.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:36.280
We'll explain everything to the school,
and I'll apologize along with you.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.780
And of course
I'll be by your side, too!

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.500
You did take a plunge into the sea,
so you should get checked out at the infirmary.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.000
Aye.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:52.960
What's wrong, Rin?

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.510
Not going to play with the others?

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:03.770
I-I took a psychology test just now
and it said my personality was...

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:07.100
...the serious type, yet indecisive!

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.060
What?

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:15.490
I think they're right. After all,
my life's been nothing but a "run-run life."

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:17.740
A "run-run life"?

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:20.450
Yeah. For example, in elementary school,

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.620
I did a "test of courage" with my friends.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.210
A cat!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.380
But I fled, leaving them behind!

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:34.050
It's always like that.
Before I know it, I'm running away.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.060
At times like that,
I look out at the sea all by myself..

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.480
Oddly enough, that calmed me down.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.610
That's how I came to love the sea.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.650
Guts, Tama, guts.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:59.910
I wanted to become a Blumer, because
if you're on a ship, there's nowhere to run.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:58.410
Aye.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.990
I thought I could finally stop this run-run life.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:06.120
But in the end, I made the entire ship run away.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.960
I don't think running away is a bad thing.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.960
After all, we're safe,
even after being through three battles.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:16.340
It's because you got us away, Rin.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:19.970
You measure the circumstances
with precision and escape if need be.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.850
Maybe that's your strong point.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:24.220
Copacetic.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.020
You can get back to work.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:27.600
You're A-OK, Tama!

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:28.940
Aye.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.730
- Squeak, squeak.
- Don't touch it.

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:35.820
It was found on some driftage
so it may be carrying a disease.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.660
Are you going to dissect it or something?

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:48.080
- L-L-L-Let's go, Tama!
- Aye.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:12.150
The Musashi is cruising along steadily, huh?

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:14.150
I just hope they're all safe.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.150
They fired at us!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.910
What? Why? What is going—

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.160
Message from Ship Four!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.200
The engine was hit! They've been crippled!

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.000
I repeat, the engine was hit! They're crippled!

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.540
I'm signalling to them with lights,
but there's no response!

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.300
Do they mistakenly perceive us as a threat?

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.300
Ship Two, approach and call out to them!

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:47.060
<i>Musashi students,
I'm an instructor at Toumai High School.</i>

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:51.810
<i>We're here to protect you.
Stop the ship and follow our instructions—</i>

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.770
Hurry! Waterproof the ship!

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.200
Let's make them stop attacking.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:08.700
If we open a hole somewhere and make it tilt,
they can't use their artillery anymore.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:12.580
That would mean firing on a student ship.

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.960
We'll safeguard the students
after we disable their artillery.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:18.210
Roger.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:21.050
Prepare for anti-surface warfare.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:23.170
Preparing for anti-surface warfare!

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.180
Main battery is in position!

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:27.970
All crew members are at their positions!
Emergency lockdown in effect!

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.680
Anti-surface warfare ready!

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.440
Ship Three has been hit!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.150
Anti-surface warfare, torpedo launch,
commence fire!

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:38.820
Launch the torpedo!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:01.840
Direct hit!

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:03.210
The target...

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.640
...has not slowed down!
Their main battery is moving!

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.760
Training ammunition won't stop them?

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.400
<i>This is your captain, Misaki!</i>

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.360
<i>All classmates, please gather
right now near the prow on the foredeck!</i>

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:22.780
<i>That's all!</i>

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.070
I wonder what's happening.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:28.530
Why did you suddenly summon everyone?

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:31.950
Listen, everyone. Right now...

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.870
...we're going to have a welcome party for Mi!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.000
F-For me?

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.130
Come to think of it, we haven't done it yet.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.760
Yeah, yeah! Let's do it up!

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.920
I'll light the candles now.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.890
- S-So is this why people were avoiding me?
- Nevermind the details!

00:14:55.980 --> 00:15:00.610
Now let's have a few words
from our new comrade, Mi!

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.740
Um, crew members of the Harekaze...

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:10.030
The Harekaze is a decidedly strange ship.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:12.910
You're lax about hierarchical relations.
There's no discipline.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.910
The captain doesn't act like a captain at all.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.660
- You think so?
- No objections.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.250
I've never seen such a slipshod ship.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.460
But...

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:29.550
L-Like Heppenheim's Starkenburg Castle,
this ship is small, but has a little charm.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:32.510
Um, the comparison is hard to understand.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.810
Then it's like Nuremberg sausage!

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:38.890
Besides, you welcomed me like this.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:41.860
Crew members of the Harekaze,

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:46.440
I am damn appreciative
of this warm welcome!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:55.290
Alright! Now let's all eat cake!

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:56.450
No objections!

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:04.250
Mina, why do you say "washi" for "I" ?

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:08.050
Is it strange? I learned it
from watching Japanese movies.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:10.970
Oh, they must've been gangster movies.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:14.050
"We're the ones who row this boat!

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:18.220
If you think you can get it to move by itself,
go ahead!"

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.140
"I'll blow this place to smithereens!"

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:22.100
Like that.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:25.110
Anyway, this cake is delicious.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.030
These are mementos.

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:28.230
Have them.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:28.990
BIG

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:29.860
CATCH

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:32.610
Danke schoen.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:35.910
Have you seen the whole movie series?

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:36.830
I sure did.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.750
I love the fourth one best!

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:44.380
The summit plan. That was a great one.
The shooting in that one hits like this...

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.040
Cute.

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:46.630
Captain... Misaki, is that you
when you were a child?

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.380
Bam! Bam!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.630
But nobody died right away.

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:49.880
Yeah. Our graduation ceremony photo.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:49.920
They'd just keep rolling around.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.880
Yeah, I love how stubborn they are.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:51.880
We were always together.

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:54.760
Is she the captain of the Musashi?

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:55.760
Although they die in the end.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.930
Yeah, that's right. The Musashi.

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:57.140
That's so great, right?

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:00.890
<i>Captain! We have
an emergency message from the school!</i>

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:02.440
What's going on?

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.770
All crew members to your stations!

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:08.900
What's the message?

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:13.780
"At northern latitude of 19.41 degrees,
eastern longitude of 145.0 degrees,

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:17.910
we lost contact with the Toumai High
instructor ship while searching for the Musashi.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:23.540
<i>Since the Harekaze is the closest ship in the area,
go to the location and report the situation."</i>

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:29.380
<i>Battle is forbidden, but make
your own safety the first priority. That is all."</i>

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:31.880
The Musashi... is this close.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:34.550
Our orders are only to report the situation.

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:36.220
Right.

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:38.640
Prepare to depart!

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.180
Raise the anchor!

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:45.020
Both sides, forward, high speed,
steady as she goes! Keep your eyes wide open!

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.190
Eight reinforcement ships have arrived!
They're in tactical formation!

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.540
Amazing. A little too much.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:17.510
They get a direct hit from being so far away.
What if we get targeted by that...

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:23.020
And the handling. A huge ship like that,
changing course in a matter of seconds.

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:24.770
Why?

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:26.850
Why is this happening?

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.270
Moka!

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.440
Shiro.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:35.030
Sorry, but would you take over?

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.240
I'm...

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.030
...going over there.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.910
Going where?

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.660
To the Musashi.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.670
Don't say stupid things.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:50.960
We already grasped the situation.
Our first priority is to report!

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.210
Enough already!

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:56.970
In what world does a captain neglect her ship

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:59.260
<i>and rushes out whenever there's danger?</i>

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:01.470
<i>Aren't comrades at sea all family?</i>

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:04.220
<i>Aren't the crew members
of this ship your family?</i>

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:06.100
<i>Well? Answer me!</i>

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:12.360
Isn't this... the home you should protect?

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:19.570
Moka... My childhood friend is over there.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:24.370
She's my dear... best friend.

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:27.710
Get the Harekaze
out of the Musashi's range immediately!

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.750
Misaki.

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:40.680
Damn it!

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.640
Hard left rudder!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.560
H-Hard left rudder!

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:48.980
We'll keep our distance between the Musashi,
and follow the skipper's movements!

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:51.560
We have to retrieve our captain, right?

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.150
Otherwise, we'd be
turning around and running!

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.610
Medical personnel, be in full readiness.

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:59.650
If you need more people,
have Budgeting lend a hand!

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:01.870
Send notifications to each department!

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:05.870
No matter what, we have to
at least stop their movement.

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:08.370
Launch the torpedo!

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:16.880
What?!

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:20.010
Vice-principal! We've lost contact
with the reinforcement fleet!

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:21.890
The data link's dead, too!

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:23.010
Get it back up!

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:24.680
- Impossible! What has—
- Incoming!

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:24.430
We're in the black!

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:31.390
The Musashi's main battery
is turning towards us!

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.070
Damn them!

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.400
Hard right rudder, steady as she goes!

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:37.280
Turn away from the Musashi!

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:38.230
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:41.950
You're doing great not running away today!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:42.780
Aye.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:47.290
We have to have the captain... Misaki,
be able to come back!

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:50.660
I got something! Three shells
from the main battery heading this way!

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.290
Incoming to the starboard bow in ten seconds!

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:54.830
They read our movement?

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.540
340 degrees, and 60.

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.920
Fire? We need to fire!

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:02.800
Shells... get hit with shells.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:05.760
Set 340 degrees, high angle 60 degrees!

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.810
Turning the turret!
Turned! 340 degrees.

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:10.560
Going with a big boom!

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:18.440
Nice one, Gunner! Your firing
of 10 cm shells is so fast!

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:21.490
- We can keep firing!
- The shells are heading straight for us!

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:25.030
- Hard right rudder! Turn inward!
- We won't make it!

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.120
350 degrees! Fire!

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:39.300
Our lead shot hit their lead shot.

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:41.510
- Yes! Yes! We did it!
- Aye.

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:42.670
- Yeay!
- Ayyye.

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:54.730
Moka!

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:18.710
Moka!

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:25.050
Episode 5: Pinched by the Musashi!
